 "title": "Growl Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: a growling, gnarly bass: the filter moving so fast it becomes a snarl rather than a wobble.\n\nHow it's built: a saw through the Ladder filter with RESONANCE up; an LFO at 22 Hz (almost too fast to hear as movement) shakes the CUTOFF, which roughens the tone into a growl; an envelope opens the filter at the start of each note; Drive. One voice.\n\nPlay: long, low notes.\n\nTweak: the LFO's RATE (slower turns the growl into a wobble, faster into a buzz), the filter's CV (how hard it growls), DRIVE.",
